      "notes": "One surface with two clients. Providers: rsa-generated (RS256/384/512, PS256/384/512; 1024, 2048 default, 4096), rsa-enc-generated (RSA1_5, RSA-OAEP, RSA-OAEP-256), ecdsa-generated (ES256/384/512; P-256 default, P-384, P-521), ecdh-generated (ECDH-ES and ECDH-ES+AnKW), eddsa-generated (Ed25519 default, Ed448), hmac-generated (HS256/384/512), aes-generated, rsa and rsa-enc (imported PEM), java-keystore (JKS or PKCS#12; BCFKS in FIPS mode). A new realm gets rsa-generated (RS256, 2048), rsa-enc-generated (RSA-OAEP), hmac-generated (HS512) and aes-generated. 'export' covers public keys and certificates only. Rotation is by adding a provider and changing priority. No ML-DSA or ML-KEM provider exists; ML-DSA signing is tracked in epic #43690 (milestone 27.0). Key material is persisted in the database in plaintext (#39933, open)."
    }
